   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 10 of the law of 1958, relating to incorporating the\nIslip Terrace Volunteer Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, and providing\nfor its powers and duties, in relation to making technical amendments thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S9977",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9977-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1, 2 & 7, Chap 10 of 1958",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters' Benevolent Association",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9977\n\nSPONSOR: WEIK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 10 of the law of 1958, relating to incorporating\nthe Islip Terrace Volunteer Exempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, and\nproviding for its powers and duties, in relation to making technical\namendments thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo update statutory language relating to the Islip Terrace Volunteer\nExempt Firemen's Benevolent Association, including gender-neutral termi-\nnology and conforming references to current provisions of law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends section 1,2, and 7 of chapter 10 of the laws of 1958 to\nupdate the name of the association by replacing \"Firemen\" with \"Fire-\nfighter's\", revise gender specific terminology throughout, and update\nreferences to Insurance Law. This section also revises provisions relat-\ning to the use of certain insurance tax revenues.\n\nSection 2 provides that the act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill updates the governing law of the Islip Terrace Volunteer\nExempt Firemen's Benevolent Association to reflect gender-neutral and\ninclusive language by replacing terms such as \"Firemen's\", \"firemen,\"\nand \"his\" with \"firefighter's\", \"firefighter,\" and \"their.\" These chang-\nes are consistent with New York State's gender-neutral standards.\n\nThis bill also revises provisions relating to the use of foreign fire\ninsurance premium tax funds received from the New York State Insurance\nDepartment. Current law limits the use of such funds to the care and\nrelief of disabled or indigent volunteer and exempt firefighters and\ntheir families. This legislation would instead allow the funds to be\nused in furtherance of all statutory purposes of the association,\nincluding maintaining a headquarters, promoting fraternal engagement\namong members, supporting the welfare of the volunteer fire service, and\ncontinuing to provide aid and assistance to members and their families.\n\nIn addition, the bill updates reference to the Insurance Law to ensure\nconsistency with current section 9104 and 9105. These changes are like\nupdates made for other volunteer firefighter's benevolent associations\nand will all the association to more effectively support its members and\ncarry out its purposes.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
